{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KuUwjLT9ALoYWCy6DeFHXU","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"liquid lithium self-diffusion coefficient experimental NMR Murday Cotts temperature dependence cm2/s\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"link.springer.com\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00883553\"},{\"title\":\"r m cotts 1Z8Qzy\",\"url\":\"https://scite.ai/authors/r-m-cotts-1Z8Qzy\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion coefficients of ionic liquids measured by multinuclear benchtop NMR\",\"url\":\"https://magritek.com/?p=21016\"},{\"title\":\"self diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.xjtu.edu.cn/en/publications/self-diffusion-coefficient-study-of-liquid-lithium/\"},{\"title\":\"s00231 011 0874 9\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00231-011-0874-9\"},{\"title\":\"ecs.confex.com\",\"url\":\"https://ecs.confex.com/ecs/imlb2016/webprogram/Paper76763.html\"},{\"title\":\"subject:Self diffusion coefficients\",\"url\":\"https://fitforthem.unipa.it/subject:Self-diffusion coefficients\"},{\"title\":\"link.aps.org\",\"url\":\"https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PhysRevB.83.094302\"},{\"title\":\"Study of transport processes in Li-ion electrolytes by Multi-nuclear diffusion NMR\",\"url\":\"https://magritek.com/2020/09/21/study-of-transport-processes-in-li-ion-electrolytes-by-multi-nuclear-diffusion-nmr/\"},{\"title\":\"next.sciencegate.app\",\"url\":\"https://next.sciencegate.app/document/10.1557/opl.2012.1517\"}]\n\nThe search did not return the Murday and Cotts liquid-lithium temperature equation or its numerical values, so I can't confirm the cm²/s figures you're after.\n\n- **Murday & Cotts (1968):** A reference list cites their paper, \"Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium,\" in J Chem Phys 48:4938–4945 (Murday JS, Cotts RM (1968) Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium. J Chem Phys 48:4938–4945). I did not retrieve its data.\n- **Later comparison:** A 2012 molecular-dynamics study reports that calculated self-diffusion coefficient is in good agreement with Murday's experiment results in atmosphere, and it fits an Arrhenius form to its simulation results (We get the Arrhenius equation according to the simulation results.). That paper is a useful cross-check, but I didn't see its fitted numbers.\n- **Other experimental work:** Feinauer, Majer and Seeger (1994) report experimental data on 6Li and 7Li diffusivities, and Ominia (2006) covers self-diffusion and inter-diffusion coefficients of liquid lithium isotopes.\n- **Caution on a nearby result:** A Springer paper gives a self-diffusion expression with D₀ = 0.038 cm²/s and Q = 12.0 kcal/mol, but it concerns the 7Li nuclear spin relaxation time T1 in solid lithium, not the liquid. Don't use it for the liquid-phase coefficient.\n\nTo get the actual liquid-phase temperature dependence, the next step is to find the full text of the Murday & Cotts 1968 paper or the Feinauer/Seeger or Ominia data sets.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"369989ee-71bc-4bad-aff4-8d3a893f64bb","uuid":"24ccdeb5-65af-4685-9edc-b5a8b2c29339","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:58:09.659Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"liquid lithium self-diffusion coefficient experimental NMR Murday Cotts temperature dependence cm2/s","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01GpTKhMTETrxFf1z6aKX3jN","content":[{"title":"link.springer.com","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00883553"},{"title":"r m cotts 1Z8Qzy","url":"https://scite.ai/authors/r-m-cotts-1Z8Qzy"},{"title":"Self-diffusion coefficients of ionic liquids measured by multinuclear benchtop NMR","url":"https://magritek.com/?p=21016"},{"title":"self diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium","url":"https://scholar.xjtu.edu.cn/en/publications/self-diffusion-coefficient-study-of-liquid-lithium/"},{"title":"s00231 011 0874 9","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00231-011-0874-9"},{"title":"ecs.confex.com","url":"https://ecs.confex.com/ecs/imlb2016/webprogram/Paper76763.html"},{"title":"subject:Self diffusion coefficients","url":"https://fitforthem.unipa.it/subject:Self-diffusion coefficients"},{"title":"link.aps.org","url":"https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PhysRevB.83.094302"},{"title":"Study of transport processes in Li-ion electrolytes by Multi-nuclear diffusion NMR","url":"https://magritek.com/2020/09/21/study-of-transport-processes-in-li-ion-electrolytes-by-multi-nuclear-diffusion-nmr/"},{"title":"next.sciencegate.app","url":"https://next.sciencegate.app/document/10.1557/opl.2012.1517"}]},"The search did not return the Murday and Cotts liquid-lithium temperature equation or its numerical values, so I can't confirm the cm²/s figures you're after.\n\n- **Murday & Cotts (1968):** A reference list cites their paper, \"Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium,\" in J Chem Phys 48:4938–4945 (Murday JS, Cotts RM (1968) Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium. J Chem Phys 48:4938–4945). I did not retrieve its data.\n- **Later comparison:** A 2012 molecular-dynamics study reports that calculated self-diffusion coefficient is in good agreement with Murday's experiment results in atmosphere, and it fits an Arrhenius form to its simulation results (We get the Arrhenius equation according to the simulation results.). That paper is a useful cross-check, but I didn't see its fitted numbers.\n- **Other experimental work:** Feinauer, Majer and Seeger (1994) report experimental data on 6Li and 7Li diffusivities, and Ominia (2006) covers self-diffusion and inter-diffusion coefficients of liquid lithium isotopes.\n- **Caution on a nearby result:** A Springer paper gives a self-diffusion expression with D₀ = 0.038 cm²/s and Q = 12.0 kcal/mol, but it concerns the 7Li nuclear spin relaxation time T1 in solid lithium, not the liquid. Don't use it for the liquid-phase coefficient.\n\nTo get the actual liquid-phase temperature dependence, the next step is to find the full text of the Murday & Cotts 1968 paper or the Feinauer/Seeger or Ominia data sets."],"durationSeconds":6.578977449999998,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KuUwjLT9ALoYWCy6DeFHXU","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016fMKn74aKTeW9PkAf1ddgz","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"liquid lithium density temperature correlation g/cm3 800 K\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"ntrs.nasa.gov\",\"url\":\"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/api/citations/19680018893/downloads/19680018893.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"repo.qst.go.jp\",\"url\":\"https://repo.qst.go.jp/records/47902\"},{\"title\":\"LITHIUM (Li)\",\"url\":\"https://qedfusion.org/LIB/PROPS/PANOS/li.html\"},{\"title\":\"repo.qst.go.jp\",\"url\":\"https://repo.qst.go.jp/records/47902/export/json\"},{\"title\":\"wulixb.iphy.ac.cn\",\"url\":\"https://wulixb.iphy.ac.cn/article/doi/10.7498/aps.55.76\"},{\"title\":\"Operational conditions:\",\"url\":\"https://www.chemeo.com/mid/22-277-a/Choline-chloride_Urea_lithium-chloride\"},{\"title\":\"Lithium chloride · LiCl\",\"url\":\"https://processconvert.pages.dev/substances/lithium-chloride\"},{\"title\":\"densite et temperature de cristallisation d une solution aqueuse de 22391\",\"url\":\"https://iifiir.org/fr/fridoc/densite-et-temperature-de-cristallisation-d-une-solution-aqueuse-de-22391\"},{\"title\":\"Contents - Index\",\"url\":\"https://fchartsoftware.com/ees/libr_help/hs400.htm\"},{\"title\":\"elogim.com\",\"url\":\"https://springerlink.bibliotecabuap.elogim.com/content/pdf/10.1361/105497198770341761.pdf\"}]\n\nI didn't find a published liquid lithium density value at 800 K, but two sources give usable correlations.\n\n- **NASA correlation (1968 report):** A NASA report correlated liquid lithium properties as a function of temperature, using both experimental data and theoretical analyses, and extrapolated them to about 1600 K. Its density is a linear fit, which the authors chose because a cubic fit gave a minimum near 1600 K. I did not get the coefficients, so this source supports the method but not a number.\n- **QED Fusion lithium page:** This page gives a cubic density fit in g/cm³ with T* = T − 271.7 and coefficients 0.5082, −1.0336×10⁻⁴, −4.8279×10⁻¹⁰, and −5.2853×10⁻¹² (Empirical equations for some physical and thermal properties of Lithium as a function of temperature are as follows). The page does not state the temperature units clearly. My own arithmetic gives about 0.48 g/cm³ at 800 K if T is in kelvin, and about 0.45 g/cm³ if the input is 800 °C. Check the units against the original reference before using either value.\n\nNeither source confirms the 800 K value directly, so verify the correlation's temperature basis before relying on the result.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"369989ee-71bc-4bad-aff4-8d3a893f64bb","uuid":"04d700b2-ed94-4df5-8f02-949dd2b2b18b","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:58:13.003Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"liquid lithium density temperature correlation g/cm3 800 K","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_015vazGNx3K25vUMhSWwi1Ad","content":[{"title":"ntrs.nasa.gov","url":"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/api/citations/19680018893/downloads/19680018893.pdf"},{"title":"repo.qst.go.jp","url":"https://repo.qst.go.jp/records/47902"},{"title":"LITHIUM (Li)","url":"https://qedfusion.org/LIB/PROPS/PANOS/li.html"},{"title":"repo.qst.go.jp","url":"https://repo.qst.go.jp/records/47902/export/json"},{"title":"wulixb.iphy.ac.cn","url":"https://wulixb.iphy.ac.cn/article/doi/10.7498/aps.55.76"},{"title":"Operational conditions:","url":"https://www.chemeo.com/mid/22-277-a/Choline-chloride_Urea_lithium-chloride"},{"title":"Lithium chloride · LiCl","url":"https://processconvert.pages.dev/substances/lithium-chloride"},{"title":"densite et temperature de cristallisation d une solution aqueuse de 22391","url":"https://iifiir.org/fr/fridoc/densite-et-temperature-de-cristallisation-d-une-solution-aqueuse-de-22391"},{"title":"Contents - Index","url":"https://fchartsoftware.com/ees/libr_help/hs400.htm"},{"title":"elogim.com","url":"https://springerlink.bibliotecabuap.