{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SCGzLgoCxUt6moKohi5Bui","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"liquid lithium\" self-diffusion \"Murday\" \"Cotts\" D0 activation energy kcal/mol 6.4 x 10^-5 cm2/s melting point\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"(PDF) Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/289594580_Self-diffusion_coefficient_of_liquid_lithium\"},{\"title\":\"Self-Diffusion Coefficient of Liquid Lithium - ADS\",\"url\":\"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1968JChPh..48.4938M/abstract\"},{\"title\":\"Towards atomistic simulations of the SEI in Li metal batteries\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/s41313-026-00092-6\"},{\"title\":\"Isotope Inter‐Diffusion and Self‐Diffusion in Solid Lithium Metal\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/229874770_Isotope_Inter-Diffusion_and_Self-Diffusion_in_Solid_Lithium_Metal\"},{\"title\":\"Li self-diffusion in pure and doped β-LiAl using pulsed-field gradient NMR - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/0022369785900927\"},{\"title\":\"Local Structure Dictates Ionic Transport and Mechanical Properties in Glassy Solid Electrolytes for Lithium Batteries\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.06895\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion in garnet-type Li7La3Zr2O12 solid electrolytes\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7801511/\"},{\"title\":\"1 Vol.:(0123456789) Scientific Reports\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-020-79919-2.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion in garnet-type Li7La3Zr2O12 solid electrolytes\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-020-79919-2\"}]\n\nThe search turned up the original 1968 Murday and Cotts paper, and its figures don't match the numbers in your query.\n\n- **Melting-point diffusion:** The ADS abstract reports that at the melting point D = 6.8 ± 0.3 × 10-5cm2 / sec and (T / D) (dD / dT) = 2.8 ± 0.3. Your query's 6.4 × 10^-5 cm²/s doesn't appear in these results.\n- **Activation energy:** The same abstract gives D = 0.94 ± 0.4 × 10-3 exp [ - (2300 ± 300cal) / RT]cm2 / sec. That implies an activation energy of about 2.3 kcal/mol, not 6.4.\n- **Conflicting values:** A ResearchGate copy of a related reference gives a different fit for liquid Li. It states that for liquid Li, the results of two investigations (195 to 440°C) have been combined, yielding 10 DOL1 = 1.44 (+ 0.07, −0.06) and QL1 = 2.87 ± 0.07. That is a combined fit from two studies, not the Murday–Cotts result alone, so it is a separate figure.\n- **Author name:** One source spells the first author \"Murdy,\" but the paper is by J.S. Murday and R.M. Cotts, published in J. Chem. Phys. 48 (1968), 4938–4945.\n\nThe results did not include a melting point value for liquid lithium itself, so I can't confirm that part of your query. The 6.4 figures may come from a different paper or a transcription error, and I'd recommend checking the original paper before relying on them.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"369989ee-71bc-4bad-aff4-8d3a893f64bb","uuid":"0b9b3e12-5e5c-47e8-bc9d-b428c9674937","timestamp":"2026-10-31T23:04:17.781Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"\"liquid lithium\" self-diffusion \"Murday\" \"Cotts\" D0 activation energy kcal/mol 6.4 x 10^-5 cm2/s melting point","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01JdXFCWKrKZ4cbzL1NEq2Yz","content":[{"title":"(PDF) Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/289594580_Self-diffusion_coefficient_of_liquid_lithium"},{"title":"Self-Diffusion Coefficient of Liquid Lithium - ADS","url":"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1968JChPh..48.4938M/abstract"},{"title":"Towards atomistic simulations of the SEI in Li metal batteries","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/s41313-026-00092-6"},{"title":"Isotope Inter‐Diffusion and Self‐Diffusion in Solid Lithium Metal","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/229874770_Isotope_Inter-Diffusion_and_Self-Diffusion_in_Solid_Lithium_Metal"},{"title":"Li self-diffusion in pure and doped β-LiAl using pulsed-field gradient NMR - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/0022369785900927"},{"title":"Local Structure Dictates Ionic Transport and Mechanical Properties in Glassy Solid Electrolytes for Lithium Batteries","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.06895"},{"title":"Self-diffusion in garnet-type Li7La3Zr2O12 solid electrolytes","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7801511/"},{"title":"1 Vol.:(0123456789) Scientific Reports","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-020-79919-2.pdf"},{"title":"Self-diffusion in garnet-type Li7La3Zr2O12 solid electrolytes","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-020-79919-2"}]},"The search turned up the original 1968 Murday and Cotts paper, and its figures don't match the numbers in your query.\n\n- **Melting-point diffusion:** The ADS abstract reports that at the melting point D = 6.8 ± 0.3 × 10-5cm2 / sec and (T / D) (dD / dT) = 2.8 ± 0.3. Your query's 6.4 × 10^-5 cm²/s doesn't appear in these results.\n- **Activation energy:** The same abstract gives D = 0.94 ± 0.4 × 10-3 exp [ - (2300 ± 300cal) / RT]cm2 / sec. That implies an activation energy of about 2.3 kcal/mol, not 6.4.\n- **Conflicting values:** A ResearchGate copy of a related reference gives a different fit for liquid Li. It states that for liquid Li, the results of two investigations (195 to 440°C) have been combined, yielding 10 DOL1 = 1.44 (+ 0.07, −0.06) and QL1 = 2.87 ± 0.07. That is a combined fit from two studies, not the Murday–Cotts result alone, so it is a separate figure.\n- **Author name:** One source spells the first author \"Murdy,\" but the paper is by J.S. Murday and R.M. Cotts, published in J. Chem. Phys. 48 (1968), 4938–4945.\n\nThe results did not include a melting point value for liquid lithium itself, so I can't confirm that part of your query. The 6.4 figures may come from a different paper or a transcription error, and I'd recommend checking the original paper before relying on them."],"durationSeconds":6.27784922600002,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SCGzLgoCxUt6moKohi5Bui","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
